  "prediction": "PIXEL-INERT, FULL SWEEP (re-registration of forzadecay414-fix-pixels.json, whose pair split Thor/Nova and failed only on Stencil/Stencil_REPLACE_ST and Stencil_REPLACE_ST_ZB, 0 -> 30000). Stencil/* is run but excluded from must_not_move under tracker #79: it flakes about 8.6% per capture-run on every binary (the guest-to-PGRAPH vertex skew), is bimodal 0/30000 on one apk on one device (rendermode474-966088, both request ids), and #79 says Stencil/* must not be used as a must_not_move control. Every other capture is held to the same claim. B is A (master 85347ffbd1) plus one change in vk/surface.c: pgraph_vk_drain_deferred_surface_releases(r, frame), which runs only once that slot's fence has been waited (the frame rotation, pgraph_vk_flush_all_frames for slots other than the current one, and the finalizers), now also sets invalidation_frame = -1 on every surface in r->invalid_surfaces stamped with that slot. Only surface_in_flight() reads invalidation_frame, and only to keep an invalid surface out of get_any_compatible_invalid_surface() and prune_invalid_surfaces(). So B changes which invalid surface images are recycled or destroyed and when; it changes no draw, copy, upload or download, and a recycled image is a render target whose content the next draw defines (the same as an image recycled after a flush_all_frames, which every title did before #517). Prediction: every capture on all 100 golden suites is byte-identical between A and B within the run-to-run band measured by 2 runs per arm; 0 better, 0 worse. RenderTextureLoop is skipped as in every arm since #379. Falsifier, and the world it fails in: a capture that moves outside its band, a validation error, device-lost or crash line in B's logcat and not A's. That is the world where a surface was still referenced by a submitted command buffer after its slot's fence was waited -- a surface drawn in one slot's CB and read by a later slot's CB without a new stamp -- so B recycled an image in use and a later draw overwrote a region a pending read still needed; it shows first in Texture_render_target, Texture_render_update_in_place, Texture_Framebuffer_Blit, Surface_format, Color_zeta_overlap and Surface_clip. Rows scored unreadable are VOID, not exact.",
